ImmutableFactory
├── fixed implementation
│   ├── constructor stores creation bytecode without constructor arguments using SSTORE2
│   ├── implementationPointer exposes the immutable SSTORE2 address for reading creation bytecode
│   ├── every instance runs that creation bytecode with the supplied ABI arguments
│   ├── preserve creation bytecode and appended arguments up to the 24,575-byte code-storage size limit
│   ├── SSTORE2 rejects larger creation bytecode with DeploymentFailed under the EVM code-size limit
│   ├── empty fixed bytecode permits complete creation bytecode in create arguments
│   └── separate logical types use separate factories and registries
├── successful create
│   ├── any caller can deploy
│   ├── append static and dynamic constructor arguments unchanged
│   ├── constructor sees the factory as its caller
│   ├── register the deployed address and emit AddEntity
│   ├── deploy at the address predicted from the current factory nonce
│   ├── repeated arguments create distinct ordinary contracts
│   ├── deploy RecipeCapability without constructor arguments and retain self-call checks
│   ├── retain self-call authorization on constructorless guarded capabilities
│   └── deploy Executor with explicit owner and immutable adapter
├── failed create
│   ├── replace constructor revert data with DeploymentFailed
│   ├── replace 32 KiB of constructor revert data with DeploymentFailed and preserve the nonce
│   ├── reject failures without revert data with DeploymentFailed
│   ├── reject malformed constructor arguments with DeploymentFailed
│   ├── reject empty runtime code with DeploymentFailed
│   └── roll back registry membership and CREATE nonce
└── isolated deterministic gas snapshots
    ├── create an executor, constructorless capability, and dynamic-argument instance
    ├── append a subsequent instance to an existing registry
    └── reject constructor reverts, large revert data, malformed arguments, and empty runtime code
